  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Two new machine conditions select two new Agie work qualities:\n  - `AGIE_COBRA_RA030` requests `CCD030`: Ra 0.30, a main cut and three trims.\n  - `AGIE_COBRA_RA070` requests `CCD070`: Ra 0.70, a main cut and two trims.\n- `agie_setup::Quality` gets `Ccd030` and `Ccd070`. Each has its measured 40 mm offsets:\n  - CCD030: 250, 170, 145 and 135 µm.\n  - CCD070: 245, 165 and 140 µm.\n- `Quality::wire()` gives the native wire name. The piece and each work write `ID_THREAD` from it. A Cobra job writes `Cobra Cut D 0.25` two times and no `Berco`.\n- The clearance and miter checks use the rough (first) offset of the selected quality.\n- The operator review names the wire, the offsets and the number of TECCUT passes.\n- Refusals. No file is written for these:\n  - The encoder refuses other heights with `SetupError::UnqualifiedCobraHeight`.\n  - The post refuses a die opening, an open cutoff, a punch group and a DXF arc punch. The group and arc refusal now names the selected condition and its height.\n- The 1 mm separation is unchanged.\n- The user guide and the site page have a new Cobra Cut D section.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2986-agie-cobra-40.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe native post knew only Berco Cut 0.25 qualities. It wrote the wire as a fixed string at piece and work level.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (both red before the fix):\n- `camcraft-post` lib `agie::cobra_tests`:\n  - `cobra_cut_d_sets_the_wire_and_quality_of_a_40_mm_punch`. The expected SBL is the Berco 40 mm SBL with only the quality line and the two wire values replaced.\n  - `cobra_cut_d_refuses_other_heights_and_sides_without_files`\n  - `the_setup_encoder_holds_cobra_cut_d_to_40_mm`\n  - `cobra_cut_d_bounds_the_cut_with_its_own_rough_offset`\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native` `cobra::`. These run the CLI on the shipped examples and include a project save and load:\n  - `a_cobra_condition_requests_its_quality_and_wire_on_a_40_mm_punch`\n  - `a_cobra_condition_refuses_other_heights_without_a_directory`\n  - `a_cobra_condition_refuses_a_group_an_arc_punch_a_die_and_a_cutoff`\n  - `a_cobra_condition_with_another_wire_diameter_is_refused`. This one is a guard. It already passed before the fix, because the existing condition and tool gate refuses the mismatch.\n\nRed before the fix:\n- The post pins did not compile, because `Ccd030`, `Ccd070`, `wire()` and `UnqualifiedCobraHeight` did not exist.\n- The app pins failed with `Select AGIE_QN2 (Fine Ra 0.30 µm) or AGIE_BERCO_RA035 ...`.\n\nMutations. Each mutation was put in, run, and restored:\n1. Old `piece.rs` with the fixed Berco wire: red in the post and app wire pins.\n2. Clearance with the QN2 rough offset instead of the quality's offset: `cobra_cut_d_bounds_the_cut_with_its_own_rough_offset` red.\n3. The encoder maps Cobra to `UnqualifiedQualityHeight`: `the_setup_encoder_holds_cobra_cut_d_to_40_mm` red.\n4. The group refusal names `AGIE_BERCO_RA035`: the app refusal pin red. This mutation survived the first version of the test, so I made the test stronger.\n\nGate on the final tree (`7a68cb5b3`, base `b2afd64ed`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 361 steps, 0 failed. This includes `post suites: agie_safe_setup`, `agie_inspection`, `app suites: agie_native`, `example_catalog*`, `wire_post` and `wire_post_alias`.\n- After the gate, one test edit fixed a clippy finding. Then `cargo xtask gate test cobra --binary agie_native` passed (4 of 4) and `cargo xtask gate test quality --binary agie_native` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 1 step (release build), ok. No light twin was selected.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 75 app heavy steps. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives no heavy step to a P6 PR and no full heavy lane to any PR.\n- The branch merges cleanly with the current `upstream/main` (`878f8c2f2`). That main has no change in the touched files.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `example_catalog*`, `agie_native` and `agie_safe_setup` suites ran green, with all Berco goldens byte-equal. No new golden file was added. The tests derive the Cobra SBL from the Berco output.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real or emulated Agie control import of a Cobra job. The offsets come from the two synthetic offline jobs of the issue. They are motion values, not a surface measurement.\n- Te, Tkm and the three options of the request copy CCB030 (1.50, 1.00, three disabled). The issue gives no other values. See the decision file.\n- No UI change. The post dialog line still names only AGIE_QN2.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes the touched Agie files.\n\nChangelog: Agie Wire EDM: conditions AGIE_COBRA_RA030 and AGIE_COBRA_RA070 request qualities CCD030 (Ra 0.30) and CCD070 (Ra 0.70) with Cobra Cut D 0.25 wire for one 40 mm polygon punch. Other heights and work types are refused.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2986\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
